  "body": "Refs #324 (tracking of the milestone boards)\nClaim: ext/opus-helper1\nAuthor model: Claude Opus 5.5\n\n**Problem.** 23 lot issues stayed `status: blocked` after their last dependency merged. Six of them are M2 lots for the Mac, and eight are engine lots for outside contributors. Work that was ready looked blocked.\n\n**Cause.**\n- The label and the `### Blocked by` section were generated once, when the issues were created on 2026-10-27, and nothing updates them.\n- The label and claim workflows only run from `master` (the legacy app).\n- `LOTS.md` no longer has a status column.\n- So the transition from blocked to ready had no owner.\n\n**What changed.** `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md` only:\n- **Shared state:** the tracker row names the milestone boards #166 (M1) and #324 (M2–M4).\n- **Still manual until the workflows are on `master`:** a new step for whoever merges, done in the same work unit as closing the issue:\n  1. list the dependents of the closed lot;\n  2. check that nothing else blocks them (a capture, an ADR, an operator decision);\n  3. swap the label and rewrite `Blocked by`, or name the real blocker;\n  4. update the board line, and add a line to the audit list #326 for a PR delivered by an outside contributor.\n\nThere is no LESSONS row, because two open PRs already add row 54. The 23 issues themselves are being fixed on GitHub right now; that is not part of this PR.\n\n**Checks.** `markdownlint-cli2@0.18.1` reports 0 errors. `check-lot-deps.py` reports 153 lots and 0 violations. The `../ROADMAP.md#milestones` anchor exists on dev-swift (#325).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHAtE1bjFGqCXryLBy)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated the orchestration guide to identify the milestone boards used to track lots and their status.\n  * Clarified the steps for closing a lot: review dependent lots, check for blockers, mark eligible lots ready, or document remaining blockers.\n  * Added guidance to update the boards when a lot is closed or another lot becomes ready.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
