   "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/327?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui-dark.svg?v=3\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\" alt=\"Review in Change Stack →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- recent_review_start -->\n\nNo actionable comments were generated in the recent review.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/info.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Recent review info</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- review_info_content -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- **Source mode**: Auto\n- **Repository**: [ezzz/HFRnow](<https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow>)\n- **Branch**: [docs/orchestration-unblock](<https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/tree/docs%2Forchestration-unblock>)\n- **File**: [.coderabbit.yaml](<https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0/.coderabbit.yaml>)\n- **Commit**: [c429006](<https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/commit/c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0>)\n- **Layers**: Repository YAML\n- **Review profile**: ASSERTIVE\n- **Plan**: Advanced\n- **Run ID**: `38917dc8-080b-4b2f-bdd1-57f4250f08ac`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/git-commit-horizontal-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/git-commit-horizontal.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Commits</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between f99442de64f1558cfa2e676dc3ae25f20017549a and c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/file-plus-corner-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/file-plus-corner.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Files selected for processing: 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n* `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n**Included review availability:** This review used your included allowance. Your plan provides up to 10 included reviews per hour; 6 remain after this review.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- recent_review_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\nThe orchestration guide now links the M1 and M2–M4 milestone boards and describes how to check and update dependent lots after a lot closes.\n\n**Changes: Lot merge documentation**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Tracker links and merge steps** <br> `docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md`|The tracker entry links the M1 and M2–M4 milestone boards. The closure workflow covers checking dependent-lot blockers, marking unblocked lots ready, adding external-contributor readiness details when applicable, and updating the boards.|\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n<strong>Priority: <picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/priority-normal-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Normal</strong>\n\n**Estimated code review effort:** 2 (Simple) | ~5 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0\" -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related issues**\n\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#324` — The guide now links this milestone board and describes updating it for closed and newly ready lots.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#166` — The guide links this board and documents checking dependent lots before updating their readiness.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#295` — The documented workflow applies to this lot’s reported stale blocked status.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#208` — The workflow requires checking remaining blockers before marking a dependent lot ready.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#275` — The workflow requires checking for other blockers before marking a dependent lot ready.\n- `ezzz/HFRnow#76` — The documented workflow applies to this lot’s reported stale blocked status.\n\n**Possibly related PRs**\n\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#167](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/167) — It defines the issue-based tracker and closure process that this guide extends.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#325](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/325) — It introduces the milestone boards that the guide now links and updates.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#321](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/321) — It introduces the external-contributor readiness label and pickup guidance used by the workflow.\n\n**Suggested reviewers:** `claude`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-unassessed-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Minimal</strong> · up to <code>c4290</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `c4290`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"c4290068388362f107be580fa349c45d89189bd0\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe documentation changes align with the existing lot-status and external-pickup conventions and are ready to merge.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Architecture risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>c4290</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- architecture_review_start -->\n<!-- architecture_review_label\n### Architecture Summary\n\n**Architecture risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `c4290`\n-->\n\nThe change affects 1 system.\n\n**Changed systems:** `docs`\n\n**Architecture concerns**\nNo architecture-level concerns identified.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Review details</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n**Systems and components**\n- _observed_ — docs (service) was modified; 1 changed file maps to changed impact.\n\n**Before / after behavior**\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md: The tracker entry now links milestone boards `#166` and `#324` and states that they show lot status as todo, ongoing, or done; it previously linked only the MVP roadmap issue `#166`.\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md: Adds a manual lot-unblocking workflow for lot closures: identify open dependents whose remaining dependencies are done, check for other blockers, and, if none remain, change the status to ready and comment `Unblocked by #PR`. Engine lots marked for external contributors also receive `external: ready` and a pickup comment. Remaining blockers are reported in a comment. The workflow also updates the milestone board for the closed lot and newly ready lots.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- architecture_review_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 5</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n|         Check name         |                                             Status                                             | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|      Description Check     | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                               |\n|         Title check        | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | The title clearly and concisely describes the main documentation change: unblocking dependent lots after each merge.                                                                                      |\n|     Docstring Coverage     | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | No eligible functions found in the changed files. Skipping docstring coverage check. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff with cyclomatic complexity of at least 2. Documentat… |\n|     Linked Issues check    | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                                  |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                                  |\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Full details: Docstring Coverage</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n**Explanation**\n\nNo eligible functions found in the changed files. Skipping docstring coverage check. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff with cyclomatic complexity of at least 2. Documentation-only edits and deletions within surviving functions are included; unchanged diff context and fully deleted functions are excluded. Analyzed 0 functions across 0 files. (1 skipped: 1 unsupported.)\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Finishing Touches</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>🧪 Generate unit tests (beta)</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"6ba7b81