   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.1, ext/opus-helper1, independent of the author): REQUEST CHANGES** — head ee063a2\n\n1. **Medium — ORCHESTRATION.md:35, \"(fixed on 2026-10-29)\".** #75 (LOT-049) and #179 (LOT-087), both in #324's list of 23 lots, still carry `status: blocked` right now, so the doc claims a fix that the tracker contradicts. Fix: drop the parenthesis, or write \"being fixed, #324 § Triage\".\n2. **Medium — :36, \"whose other dependencies are all closed\".** A dependency closed as *not planned* counts as closed, and would wrongly make its dependents ready. Fix: say \"done (closed with `Done in #PR`)\". A dropped dependency is a plan change: the LOTS.md row changes first, by PR, and then the cell decides.\n3. **Medium — :38, rewriting `### Blocked by`.** This edits an issue the maintainer wrote. AGENTS.md §0 makes that an action to confirm first, and AGENTS.md §8 and EXTERNAL-AGENTS §10 list only \"close the issue\" as the merger's duty. Fix: either declare it routine under the merge policy in AGENTS.md §8 (one line, in this PR), or make the unblock a label swap plus an `Unblocked by #PR` comment, with the body edit optional.\n4. **Low — :36, gate cells.** Cells like `all parsing/network/storage lots` (LOT-070, #94) or LOT-164's 49-lot cell never name the closed lot, so the last engine merge would never make them ready. Fix: add \"a gate cell counts once its last lot is done\".\n5. **Low — :37, the blocker check.**\n   - LESSONS 35: a parser lot also needs the legacy oracle output, so add it to the check.\n   - Closing a capture issue (`host: mac`) unblocks nothing either. Fix: say that whoever closes a capture runs the same steps.\n6. **Nit — :38–39.**\n   - Nothing says when a lot gets `external: ready` (the board's 🤝 flavor, or an operator decision).\n   - \"the lot's line\" is ambiguous: the closed lot becomes ✅ and each dependent becomes 🟦.\n   - The #326 sentence belongs under the \"whoever merges closes\" bullet.\n   - With auto-merge, give the author the unblock as a to-do, like the issue closure.\n\n**Checked**\n- The diff against AGENTS.md §5, §7 and §8, and EXTERNAL-AGENTS §1, §5 and §10. Authors without write access never merge, so \"whoever merges\" is always a member: OK.\n- LESSONS 35–36.\n- \"LOTS.md never edited\": the step only reads it, which is OK.\n- `Refs #N` does not trigger the step, which is correct.\n- The `../ROADMAP.md#milestones` anchor resolves, and #166, #324 and #326 exist.\n- markdownlint-cli2 0.18.1 and `check-lot-deps.py` (153 lots) pass on ee063a2.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
